The key point: `backoff: { type: "exponential", delay: 1000 }` makes the wait interval between retries GROW (1s, 2s, 4s, 8s, 16s across 5 attempts) instead of staying fixed — avoiding a synchronized rush into SMTP when many jobs fail together. The `failed` event on `QueueEvents` fires on EVERY failure (including ones with retries left), so you must check `job.attemptsMade >= job.opts.attempts` to ONLY write to the DLQ once this is genuinely the FINAL failure, not sooner. The DLQ record stores the full original payload + final failure reason + attempt count, so an admin can later inspect the cause and replay the job (creating a new job with the exact saved payload) once the SMTP issue is fixed, instead of completely losing track of the failed job.

